Some studies have shown that AR systems that combine context-based and external environment-related data can improve passengers’ experience (Inbar and Tractinsky 2011; Matsumura and Kirk 2018). In this regard, it is necessary to design a high-level UX (User Experience) by introducing a user interface that allows passengers to observe the external environment and learn relevant information (Pfleging et al. 2016). Especially in public transportation such as buses, where passengers often look out the window, showing the location of specific buildings in augmented reality can be used as an intuitive and accurate advertisement. The augmented reality system can easily explain information about specific terrain or buildings, which can be useful in

