3.2  AR algorithms
We have implemented 3DCAR (3D Coordinate Augmented Reality), an AR algorithm for implementing location-based, depth-reflecting AR content in in-vehicle AR systems (Fig. 3). 3DCAR consists of a map editor and an AR client. The map editor stores the information of buildings on the map in a 3D coordinate system and maps AR content, and the AR client collects the location of the vehicle in real time and displays AR content around the vehicle on the screen. Each technology is described in detail below.
RTK data
