As future work, it is necessary to implement and test additional system designs such as entertainment, communication platforms, and task support, which are highly demanded by the passengers in the vehicles (Osswald et al. 2013). We expect that the effectiveness of FARS can be enhanced by combining AR content with joystick and hand tracker interactions. In addition, it is worth exploring the application of AI object recognition to detect and augment information about dynamic external environments rather than predetermined static buildings. There is also a need for UX design and further research into whether the system can have a positive impact on passengers in vehicles traveling at higher speeds. It is necessary to verify whether there is an effect on long-term memory in addition to short-term memory within FARS to further prove the effect on spatial cognition. The results of the spatial cognition study are expected to be useful not only for navigation, but also for advertising and training.
